{%- comment -%}
  Product Card — one card in the OW Landing products band.

  Exactly one `product` setting, first in the schema. That is what gives every
  other setting in this block a dynamic source scoped to this card's product,
  so each field can be connected to one of that product's metafields — or typed
  over by hand. Three products in one block, as this used to be, leaves every
  field with an ambiguous context and no per-card binding at all.

  Precedence: a text setting wins whenever it holds anything, whether typed or
  connected to a metafield; blank falls through to the product. That only works
  because these settings ship with no `default:` — pre-filled copy would win
  permanently and the product could never show through.

  Grade and flavour have no product equivalent and are not guessed from tags.
  Blank means no badge, and the element is dropped rather than rendered empty:
  both are filled colour pills, so an empty one leaves a visible stub.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign prod = block.settings.product -%}
{%- assign p_name = block.settings.name -%}
{%- if p_name == blank -%}
  {%- assign p_name = prod.title -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign p_desc = block.settings.description -%}
{%- if p_desc == blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Product descriptions are rich text and unbounded, while the card has no line
    clamp (.product-desc is flex:1) — a long one simply makes that card taller
    than the two beside it and breaks the row. The design's copy runs ~28 words,
    so 45 is generous headroom while still keeping the row even.

    A merchant-written override is left at whatever length they chose;
    truncating what someone typed into the field in front of them reads as a bug.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign p_desc = prod.description | strip_html | strip | truncatewords: 45 -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if p_name == blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    An unconfigured card. On the storefront it draws nothing; in the theme
    editor it has to stay visible and clickable, or the block a merchant just
    added would vanish from the preview with no way to select it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if request.design_mode -%}
    <div class="product-card" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
      <div class="product-card-body" style="padding:24px 16px;text-align:center;">
        <div class="product-name">Empty card</div>
        <p class="product-desc paragraph">Choose a product in Select Product to fill this card in.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
  <div class="product-card" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    <div class="product-card-img-wrap" style="position:relative">
      {%- if block.settings.grade != blank -%}
        <div class="grade-tag">{{ block.settings.grade }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
      <div class="product-card-img">
        {%- comment -%}
          The image and the title both link to the product, but only the title is
          exposed to assistive tech: two adjacent links to the same URL make a
          screen reader announce every card twice. The image's link is taken out
          of the tab order and out of the accessibility tree, which is safe
          precisely because tabindex="-1" makes it unfocusable — aria-hidden on a
          focusable element is the thing to avoid, not this.

          Rendered only when a product is actually selected; a name-only card
          would otherwise get href="" and reload the page.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if prod != blank -%}
          <a class="product-card-img-link" href="{{ prod.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if block.settings.image -%}
          {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 600 | image_tag: alt: p_name }}
        {%- elsif prod != blank and prod.featured_image -%}
          {{ prod.featured_image | image_url: width: 600 | image_tag: alt: p_name }}
        {%- else -%}
          <img src="{{ 'ow-product-card-placeholder.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="{{ p_name | escape }}" width="464" height="650">
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if prod != blank -%}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="product-card-body">
      {%- if block.settings.flavour != blank -%}
        <span class="product-tag">{{ block.settings.flavour }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <div class="product-name">
        {%- if prod != blank -%}
          <a href="{{ prod.url }}">{{ p_name }}</a>
        {%- else -%}
          {{ p_name }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- comment -%}
        Kept even when empty: .product-desc carries flex:1 and is what pushes the
        price and button to the foot of the card. Dropping it leaves a short,
        top-heavy card that no longer lines up with the two beside it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="product-desc paragraph">{{ p_desc }}</p>
      {%- if prod != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          prod.price is the lowest variant price. On a product whose variants
          differ in price that reads as a flat price, so say "From" instead of
          quietly understating it.

          Format the money value first: `t: price: prod.price | money` would
          apply money to the translated string rather than to the price.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign price_str = prod.price | money -%}
        <p class="product-price">
          {%- if prod.price_varies -%}
            {{ 'products.product.price.from_price_html' | t: price: price_str }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ price_str }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>
        {%- comment -%}
          A plain {% form 'product' %} posts to /cart/add and lands on the cart
          page. Be Yours' <product-form> custom element is deliberately not used
          here: it drives the cart drawer, which lives in the vendor header we
          replaced. The native post is the same fallback product-form.js itself
          uses when no drawer is present.

          Build the id first — a filter inside the tag's argument list is not
          scoped to that argument, and Liquid ends up reading the filtered value
          as a positional argument. It keys off the block id, so a form keeps its
          identity when cards are reordered in the editor.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign product_form_id = 'ow-product-form-' | append: block.id -%}
        {%- form 'product', prod, id: product_form_id, class: 'product-card-form' -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            A single-variant product has one variant literally titled "Default
            Title". Rendering the dropdown regardless would show that string as
            if it were a size option, so the selector is only drawn when there is
            a real choice to make; otherwise the variant id goes in a hidden
            input so the form still posts.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if prod.has_only_default_variant -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ prod.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}">
            {%- comment -%}
              The dropdown's slot is reserved even with nothing to choose, so the
              price, selector and button sit at the same height on every card in
              the row. Without it this card's footer is one row shorter and its
              price drops into the gap while its neighbours' sits higher.

              It is an empty <select> rather than a styled div so its box is
              identical to a real selector's by construction — a div has to
              reconstruct that height from a line box and lands a pixel out. It
              carries no `name`, so it contributes nothing to the form post.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <select class="product-dropdown product-dropdown--spacer" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" disabled></select>
          {%- else -%}
            <select class="product-dropdown" name="id" aria-label="{{ p_name | escape }} options">
              {%- for variant in prod.variants -%}
                <option value="{{ variant.id }}"
                        {% if variant == prod.selected_or_first_available_variant %}selected{% endif %}
                        {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
                  {{ variant.title }}
                </option>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </select>
          {%- endif -%}
          <button class="product-atc" type="submit" {% unless prod.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
            {%- if prod.available -%}{{ block.settings.atc_label }}{%- else -%}{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}{%- endif -%}
          </button>
        {%- endform -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Named but not linked. The button keeps the card's shape and reads as
          plainly unfinished, which is the honest signal to whoever is editing.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <button class="product-atc" type="button" disabled aria-disabled="true">{{ block.settings.atc_label }}</button>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product Card",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "product", "id": "product", "label": "Select Product", "info": "Drives the card image, price, variants and a working Add to Cart." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Card image", "info": "Optional. Overrides the product's featured image." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Text overrides" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Leave a field blank to use the product's own value. To override, type into it — or use the dynamic source icon beside it to connect one of this product's metafields." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Name", "info": "Blank uses the product title." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "description", "label": "Description", "info": "Blank uses the product description, trimmed to 45 words." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "grade", "label": "Grade tag", "info": "Blank hides the badge." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "flavour", "label": "Flavour tag", "info": "Blank hides the tag." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Button" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "atc_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Add to Cart" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Product Card" }]
}
{% endschema %}
